   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT authorizing Vineyard Christian Fellowship South Shore Inc. to file with\nthe county of Nassau assessor an application for a retroactive real property\ntax exemption",
    "basePrintNo": "S6426",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6426-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Nassau County",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6426\n\nSPONSOR: CANZONERI-FITZPATRICK\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act authorizing Vineyard Christian Fellowship South Shore Inc. to\nfile with the county of Nassau assessor an application for a retroactive\nreal property tax exemption\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo grant a retroactive property tax exemption for Vineyard Christian\nFellowship South Shore Inc. for the 2020-2021 assessment roll for all\nthe 2020-2021 school taxes and all the 2021 general taxes for the parcel\nconveyed to such organization located at 142 Franklin Ave, town of Hemp-\nstead, county of Nassau.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Notwithstanding any other provision of law to the contrary,\nthe assessor of the county of Nassau is hereby authorized to accept from\nVineyard Christian Fellowship South Shore Inc. application for exemption\nfrom real property taxes pursuant to section 420-a of the real property\ntax law for the 2020-2021 assessment roll for all the 2020-2021 school\ntaxes and all the 2021 general taxes for the parcel conveyed to such\norganization located at 142 Franklin Ave, town of Hempstead, county of\nNassau, otherwise known as Nassau county parcel ID section 37 block 205\nlot 335. If accepted, the application shall be reviewed as if it had\nbeen received on or before the taxable status date established for such\nrole.\n\nIf satisfied that such organization would otherwise be entitled to such\nexemption if such organization had filed an application for exemption by\nthe appropriate taxable status date, the assessor, upon approval by the\nNassau county legislature, may make appropriate correction to the\nsubject rolls. If such exemption is granted and such organization,\ntherefore, shall have paid any tax with respect to the subject rolls,\nthe applicable governing body or tax department may, in its sole\ndiscretion, provide for the refund of those taxes paid and cancel those\ntaxes, fines, penalties, liens or interest remaining unpaid.\n\nSection 2. This act shall take effect immediately.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nVineyard Christian Fellowship South Shore Inc. is a not-for-profit,\ntax-exempt religious organization. After purchasing the home located on\nat 142 Franklin Ave in July of 2020, their tax exemption papers were\nmistakenly not submitted to Nassau County. Allowing Vineyard Christian\nFellowship South Shore Inc.to be forgiven of these property tax bills\nwill allow them to continue their work in the community and keep their\nplace of worship. This legislation would allow for the Nassau County\nAssessor to accept an application for a retroactive property tax\nexemption for Vineyard Christian Fellowship South Shore Inc. and there-\nfore would relieve the current fiscal burden on this organization.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nEffective Immediately.\n",
